    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d405">

                <pb facs="0477" n="467" sameAs="frus:frus1943China/pg467"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/7707: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Atcheson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-09-02T14:00:00+07:00">September 2,
                            1943—2 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 6—8:54 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1624. Embassy’s 1550, August 24. Chairman has informed me that his resignation
                    has not been accepted, that he again told Dr. Kung he would carry on until
                    successor is named and that he accordingly expects to continue in the post for
                    some time. He stated also that question of revision continues to be discussed
                    and he intimated that he was strongly opposing revision, including any revision
                    which would eliminate foreign members of the Board. He mentioned several times
                    that the “Board has no power”.</p>
                <p>Please inform Treasury.</p>
                <p>Repeated Calcutta for Adler’s information.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Atcheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
